      "message": "init: don't wrap the default onion port to 0 for -port=65535\n\nThe default onion port is `-port` + 1, computed in `uint16_t`. With `-port=65535` it wrapped to 0, so the default onion listener bound to `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port nobody can reach) and the same port 0 was used for `-bind=<addr>=onion` without a port and as the onion service target.\n\nFail at startup with an error that asks for a lower `-port` or an explicit onion port instead. `-bind=<addr>:<port>=onion` with an explicit port keeps working.\n\nfeature_port.py gets a case for both paths; it fails on master (the node starts and binds port 0).\n\nThis patch was prepared with AI assistance (Claude) and reviewed and tested by me.",
